{:edb/committed true :edb/basis-t 1727 :edb/replayed false :edb/tx-hash "f10d02ff257dea42b3a9a4703c8cdd1ffa9c8b61151699fc434d8412837e8999" :edb/db-before-t 1726 :edb/db-after-t 1727 :edb/tx-data [[13194139535039 50 #inst "2026-10-08T15:28:59.520Z" 13194139535039 true] [17592186128918 1100 "Evaluate the repeated integral $\\displaystyle \\int_{2}^{4}  \\int_{0}^{2} \\dfrac{x^3}{y^2} \\, \\textrm{d}x  \\, \\textrm{d}y.$" 13194139535039 true] [17592186128918 1100 "Evaluate the repeated integral $\\displaystyle \\int_{2}^{4} \\int_{0}^{2} \\dfrac{x^3}{y^2} \\, \\textrm{d}x \\, \\textrm{d}y$." 13194139535039 false] [17592186128918 1145 "First, we evaluate the inner integral by integrating with respect to $x$, treating $y$ as a constant:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\n∫_{2}^{4}[∫_{0}^{2}\\frac{x^{3}}{y^{2}}dx]dy &= ∫_{2}^{4}\\frac{1}{y^{2}}[\\frac{x^{4}}{4}]_{0}^{2}dy \\\\\n&= ∫_{2}^{4}\\frac{1}{y^{2}}(\\frac{2^{4}}{4} - \\frac{0^{4}}{4})dy \\\\\n&= ∫_{2}^{4}\\frac{4}{y^{2}}dy \\\\\n&= 4∫_{2}^{4}\\frac{1}{y^{2}}dy\n\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThen, we integrate with respect to $y$:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\n4∫_{2}^{4}\\frac{1}{y^{2}}dy &= 4[- \\frac{1}{y}]_{2}^{4} \\\\\n&= 4(-\\frac{1}{4} - (-\\frac{1}{2})) \\\\\n&= 4 \\cdot \\frac{1}{4} \\\\\n&= 1\n\\end{aligned}\n$$" 13194139535039 false] [17592186128918 1145 "First, we evaluate the inner integral by integrating with respect to $x$, treating $y$ as a constant:    \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\int }_{2}^{4}[{\\int }_{0}^{2}\\frac{{x}^{3}}{{y}^{2}}\\,\\text{d}x]\\text{d}y & ={\\int }_{2}^{4}\\frac{1}{{y}^{2}}{[\\frac{{x}^{4}}{4}]}_{0}^{2}\\,\\text{d}y \\\\  & ={\\int }_{2}^{4}\\frac{1}{{y}^{2}}(\\frac{{2}^{4}}{4}-\\frac{{0}^{4}}{4})\\text{d}y \\\\  & ={\\int }_{2}^{4}\\frac{4}{{y}^{2}}\\,\\text{d}y \\\\  & =4{\\int }_{2}^{4}\\frac{1}{{y}^{2}}\\,\\text{d}y\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThen, we integrate with respect to $y\\mathbin{:}$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}4{\\int }_{2}^{4}\\frac{1}{{y}^{2}}\\,\\text{d}y & =4{[-\\frac{1}{y}]}_{2}^{4} \\\\  & =4(-\\frac{1}{4}-(-\\frac{1}{2})) \\\\  & =4\\cdot \\frac{1}{4} \\\\  & =1\\end{aligned}\n$$" 13194139535039 true] [17592186128919 1100 "Evaluate the double integral $\\displaystyle \\iint \\limits_{D} \\dfrac y{x^2} \\, \\textrm d A$, where\n$D=\\left\\{(x,y) \\:: \\:2 \\leq x \\leq 4,\\: 0 \\leq y \\leq 3\\right\\}$." 13194139535039 false] [17592186128919 1100 "Evaluate the double integral $\\displaystyle \\iint \\limits_{D} \\dfrac y{x^2} \\, \\textrm d A$, where \n$D=\\left\\{ (x,y) \\: : \\:2 \\leq x \\leq 4,\\: 0 \\leq y \\leq 3\\right\\}.$" 13194139535039 true] [17592186128919 1145 "First, we express our double integral as a repeated integral:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\n∬_(D)\\frac{y}{x^{2}}dA &= ∫_{0}^{3}[∫_{2}^{4}\\frac{y}{x^{2}}dx]dy\n\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, we evaluate the inner integral by integrating with respect to $x$, treating $y$ as a constant:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\n∫_{0}^{3}[∫_{2}^{4}\\frac{y}{x^{2}}dx]dy &= ∫_{0}^{3}[- \\frac{y}{x}]_{2}^{4}dy \\\\\n&= ∫_{0}^{3}(-\\frac{y}{4} - (-\\frac{y}{2}))dy \\\\\n&= ∫_{0}^{3}\\frac{y}{4}dy\n\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFinally, we integrate with respect to $y$:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\n∫_{0}^{3}\\frac{y}{4}dy &= [\\frac{y^{2}}{8}]_{0}^{3} \\\\\n&= \\frac{3^{2}}{8} - \\frac{0^{2}}{8} \\\\\n&= \\frac{9}{8}\n\\end{aligned}\n$$" 13194139535039 false] [17592186128919 1145 "First, we express our double integral as a repeated integral:    \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{∬}_{D}\\frac{y}{{x}^{2}}\\,\\text{d}A & ={\\int }_{0}^{3}[{\\int }_{2}^{4}\\frac{y}{{x}^{2}}\\,\\text{d}x]\\text{d}y\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, we evaluate the inner integral by integrating with respect to $x$, treating $y$ as a constant:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\int }_{0}^{3}[{\\int }_{2}^{4}\\frac{y}{{x}^{2}}\\,\\text{d}x]\\text{d}y & ={\\int }_{0}^{3}{[-\\frac{y}{x}]}_{2}^{4}\\text{d}y \\\\  & ={\\int }_{0}^{3}(-\\frac{y}{4}-(-\\frac{y}{2}))\\,\\text{d}y \\\\  & ={\\int }_{0}^{3}\\frac{y}{4}\\,\\text{d}y\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFinally, we integrate with respect to $y\\mathbin{:}$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\int }_{0}^{3}\\frac{y}{4}\\,\\text{d}y & ={[\\frac{{y}^{2}}{8}]}_{0}^{3} \\\\  & =\\frac{{3}^{2}}{8}-\\frac{{0}^{2}}{8} \\\\  & =\\frac{9}{8}\\end{aligned}\n$$" 13194139535039 true] [17592186128920 1100 "Which of the following equalities are true given that\n$D = \\big\\{ (x,y) \\: : \\: 0 \\leq x \\leq 2, \\: 0 \\leq y \\leq 1 \\big\\}.$\n\n- $\\displaystyle \\iint\\limits_{D} e^{\\sqrt{xy}} \\,\\text{d}A  = \\int_{0}^{1}  \\int_{0}^{2}e^{\\sqrt{xy}}\\,  \\text{d}y \\, \\text{d}x$\n\n- $\\displaystyle \\iint\\limits_{D} e^{\\sqrt{xy}}\\,\\text{d}A  = \\int_{0}^{2}  \\int_{0}^{1} e^{\\sqrt{xy}}\\, \\text{d}y\\,  \\text{d}x$\n\n- $\\displaystyle \\iint\\limits_{D} e^{\\sqrt{xy}} \\,\\text{d}A = \\int_{0}^{1}  \\int_{0}^{2}e^{\\sqrt{xy}}\\,  \\text{d}x \\, \\text{d}y$" 13194139535039 true] [17592186128920 1100 "Which of the following equalities are true given that\n$D = \\big\\{(x,y) \\:: \\: 0 \\leq x \\leq 2, \\: 0 \\leq y \\leq 1 \\big\\}$.\n\n1. $\\displaystyle \\iint\\limits_{D} e^{\\sqrt{xy}} \\,\\text{d}A = \\int_{0}^{1} \\int_{0}^{2}e^{\\sqrt{xy}}\\, \\text{d}y \\, \\text{d}x$\n2. $\\displaystyle \\iint\\limits_{D} e^{\\sqrt{xy}}\\,\\text{d}A = \\int_{0}^{2} \\int_{0}^{1} e^{\\sqrt{xy}}\\, \\text{d}y\\, \\text{d}x$\n3. $\\displaystyle \\iint\\limits_{D} e^{\\sqrt{xy}} \\,\\text{d}A = \\int_{0}^{1} \\int_{0}^{2}e^{\\sqrt{xy}}\\, \\text{d}x \\, \\text{d}y$" 13194139535039 false] [17592186128920 1145 "We notice that:\n\n- the limits for the variable $x$ are from ${\\color{blue}0}$ to ${\\color{blue}2}$, and\n- the limits for the variable $y$ are from ${\\color{red}0}$ to ${\\color{red}1}$.\n\nTherefore,\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\n∬_(D)e^{\\sqrt{xy}}dA &= ∫_{0}^{1}[∫_{0}^{2}e^{\\sqrt{xy}}dx]dy\n\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, since the region of integration is rectangular, we can simply swap the order of integration. This gives\n\n$$\n\\iint\\limits_{D} e^{\\sqrt{xy}} \\,\\text{d}A = \\int_{\\color{blue}0}^{\\color{blue}{2}} \\left[ \\int_{\\color{red}0}^{\\color{red}1} e^{\\sqrt{xy}}\\,\\text{d}{\\color{red}y} \\right] \\text{d}{\\color{blue}x}\n$$\n\nSo, the correct answer is \"II and III only\"." 13194139535039 false] [17592186128920 1145 "We notice that: \n\n- the limits for the variable $x$ are from ${\\color{blue}0}$ to ${\\color{blue}2}$, and\n\n- the limits for the variable $y$ are from ${\\color{red}0}$ to ${\\color{red}1}.$\n\nTherefore,\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{∬}_{D}{e}^{\\sqrt{xy}}\\,\\text{d}A & ={\\int }_{0}^{1}[{\\int }_{0}^{2}{e}^{\\sqrt{xy}}\\,\\text{d}x]\\text{d}y.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, since the region of integration is rectangular, we can simply swap the order of integration. This gives\n\n$$\n\\iint\\limits_{D} e^{\\sqrt{xy}} \\,\\text{d}A  \n= \\int_{\\color{blue}0}^{\\color{blue}{2}} \\left[ \\int_{\\color{red}0}^{\\color{red}1} e^{\\sqrt{xy}}\\,\\text{d}{\\color{red}y} \\right] \\text{d}{\\color{blue}x} .\n$$\n\nSo, the correct answer is \"II and III only\"." 13194139535039 true] [17592186129099 1020 #edb/ref 17592186328278 13194139535039 true] [17592186129099 1020 #edb/ref 17592186328285 13194139535039 true] [17592186129099 1020 #edb/ref 17592186328306 13194139535039 true] [17592186129099 1020 #edb/ref 17592186328355 13194139535039 true] [17592186129099 1020 #edb/ref 17592186328362 13194139535039 true] [17592186129100 1020 #edb/ref 17592186328327 13194139535039 true] [17592186129100 1020 #edb/ref 17592186328334 13194139535039 true] [17592186129100 1020 #edb/ref 17592186328341 13194139535039 true] [17592186129100 1020 #edb/ref 17592186328348 13194139535039 true] [17592186129100 1020 #edb/ref 17592186328369 13194139535039 true] [17592186129101 1020 #edb/ref 17592186328292 13194139535039 true] [17592186129101 1020 #edb/ref 17592186328299 13194139535039 true] [17592186129101 1020 #edb/ref 17592186328313 13194139535039 true] [17592186129101 1020 #edb/ref 17592186328320 13194139535039 true] [17592186129101 1020 #edb/ref 17592186328376 13194139535039 true] [17592186328278 1017 #edb/ref 17592186328279 13194139535039 true] [17592186328278 1089 "q-129549" 13194139535039 true] [17592186328278 1091 #edb/ref 17592186045465 13194139535039 true] [17592186328278 1100 "${\\int }_{1}^{2}{\\int }_{0}^{1}\\frac{1}{(x+y)^{2}}\\,\\text{d}x\\,\\text{d}y=$" 13194139535039 true] [17592186328278 1113 #uuid "a914a731-2557-5830-aa4d-f86a434e3214" 13194139535039 true] [17592186328278 1145 "First, we evaluate the inner integral by integrating with respect to $x$, treating $y$ as a constant. \n\nMaking a substitution $x+y=u,$ $\\text{d}x=\\text{d}u,$ we get.\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\int }_{1}^{2}{\\int }_{0}^{1}\\frac{1}{(x+y)^{2}}\\,\\text{d}x\\text{d}y & ={\\int }_{1}^{2}[{\\int }_{0}^{1}\\frac{1}{(x+y)^{2}}\\,\\text{d}x]\\text{d}y \\\\  & ={\\int }_{1}^{2}[{\\int }_{y}^{1+y}\\frac{1}{{u}^{2}}\\,\\text{d}u]\\text{d}y \\\\  & ={\\int }_{1}^{2}{[-\\frac{1}{u}]}_{y}^{1+y}\\,\\text{d}y \\\\  & ={\\int }_{1}^{2}(-\\frac{1}{y+1}+\\frac{1}{y})\\,\\text{d}y \\\\  & ={\\int }_{1}^{2}[\\frac{1}{y}-\\frac{1}{y+1}]\\,\\text{d}y\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n \n\nThen, we integrate with respect to $y:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\int }_{1}^{2}[\\frac{1}{y}-\\frac{1}{y+1}]\\,\\text{d}y & =[\\operatorname{ln}⁡y-\\operatorname{ln}⁡(y+1)]_{1}^{2} \\\\  & =\\operatorname{ln}⁡(\\frac{y}{y+1}){|}_{1}^{2} \\\\  & =\\operatorname{ln}⁡(\\frac{2}{3})-\\operatorname{ln}⁡(\\frac{1}{2}) \\\\  & =\\operatorname{ln}⁡(\\frac{2}{3})+\\operatorname{ln}⁡(2) \\\\  & =\\operatorname{ln}⁡(\\frac{2}{3}\\cdot 2) \\\\  & =\\operatorname{ln}⁡(\\frac{4}{3})\\end{aligned}\n$$" 13194139535039 true] [17592186328279 1000 #edb/ref 17592186328280 13194139535039 true] [17592186328279 1000 #edb/ref 17592186328281 13194139535039 true] [17592186328279 1000 #edb/ref 17592186328282 13194139535039 true] [17592186328279 1000 #edb/ref 17592186328283 13194139535039 true] [17592186328279 1000 #edb/ref 17592186328284 13194139535039 true] [17592186328279 1040 #edb/ref 17592186045450 13194139535039 true] [17592186328279 1041 "selection" 13194139535039 true] [17592186328279 1104 #edb/ref 17592186328284 13194139535039 true] [17592186328279 1110 #uuid "75822314-1f35-54ad-af45-1e19b05d6edd" 13194139535039 true] [17592186328280 1034 "-\\operatorname{ln}⁡(\\frac{2}{3})" 13194139535039 true] [17592186328280 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139535039 true] [17592186328280 1111 #uuid "45242f4d-4225-5667-a0e4-cc82a69c00b5" 13194139535039 true] [17592186328281 1034 "\\operatorname{ln}⁡(\\frac{1}{2})" 13194139535039 true] [17592186328281 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139535039 true] [17592186328281 1111 #uuid "2cf2214f-7fbc-5de0-bbd3-2d2d218167ed" 13194139535039 true] [17592186328282 1034 "1+\\operatorname{ln}⁡(\\frac{1}{2})" 13194139535039 true] [17592186328282 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139535039 true] [17592186328282 1111 #uuid "4d098a7e-d70f-5bc0-8921-26ca679de49f" 13194139535039 true] [17592186328283 1034 "\\operatorname{ln}⁡(\\frac{1}{2})+3" 13194139535039 true] [17592186328283 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139535039 true] [17592186328283 1111 #uuid "a5b954ca-bfb8-5f05-b794-e7483543c9f0" 13194139535039 true] [17592186328284 1034 "\\operatorname{ln}⁡(\\frac{4}{3})" 13194139535039 true] [17592186328284 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139535039 true] [17592186328284 1111 #uuid "29d05e24-e551-5cbd-9c62-39c0227ffae3" 13194139535039 true] [17592186328285 1017 #edb/ref 17592186328286 13194139535039 true] [17592186328285 1089 "q-129550" 13194139535039 true] [17592186328285 1091 #edb/ref 17592186045463 13194139535039 true] [17592186328285 1100 "${\\int }_{1}^{2}{\\int }_{0}^{\\pi /2}y\\operatorname{sin}⁡x\\,\\text{d}x\\,\\text{d}y=$" 13194139535039 true] [17592186328285 1113 #uuid "456aeadb-1a82-5da8-9100-a3eab9dc8ab8" 13194139535039 true] [17592186328285 1145 "First, we evaluate the inner integral by integrating with respect to $x$, treating $y$ as a constant: \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\int }_{1}^{2}[{\\int }_{0}^{\\pi /2}y\\operatorname{sin}⁡x\\,\\text{d}x]\\text{d}y & ={\\int }_{1}^{2}y[{\\int }_{0}^{\\pi /2}\\operatorname{sin}⁡x\\,\\text{d}x]\\text{d}y \\\\  & ={\\int }_{1}^{2}y{[-\\operatorname{cos}⁡x]}_{0}^{\\pi /2}\\,\\text{d}y \\\\  & ={\\int }_{1}^{2}y[-\\operatorname{cos}⁡(\\frac{\\pi }{2})+\\operatorname{cos}⁡0]\\,\\text{d}y \\\\  & ={\\int }_{1}^{2}y\\,\\text{d}y\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n \n\nThen, we integrate with respect to $y:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\int }_{1}^{2}y\\,\\text{d}y & ={[\\frac{{y}^{2}}{2}]}_{1}^{2} \\\\  & =\\frac{{2}^{2}}{2}-\\frac{1}{2} \\\\  & =2-\\frac{1}{2} \\\\  & =\\frac{3}{2}\\end{aligned}\n$$" 13194139535039 true] [17592186328286 1000 #edb/ref 17592186328287 13194139535039 true] [17592186328286 1000 #edb/ref 17592186328288 13194139535039 true] [17592186328286 1000 #edb/ref 17592186328289 13194139535039 true] [17592186328286 1000 #edb/ref 17592186328290 13194139535039 true] [17592186328286 1000 #edb/ref 17592186328291 13194139535039 true] [17592186328286 1040 #edb/ref 17592186045450 13194139535039 true] [17592186328286 1041 "selection" 13194139535039 true] [17592186328286 1104 #edb/ref 17592186328291 13194139535039 true] [17592186328286 1110 #uuid "e1867a25-3270-58fa-99ba-8cc80cf96a2b" 13194139535039 true] [17592186328287 1034 "\\frac{3\\pi }{2}" 13194139535039 true] [17592186328287 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139535039 true] [17592186328287 1111 #uuid "7c6ed6e9-ce09-5ea5-bc32-6f1730b18ee4" 13194139535039 true] [17592186328288 1034 "\\frac{1}{2}" 13194139535039 true] [17592186328288 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139535039 true] [17592186328288 1111 #uuid "2b50727a-c7f5-5196-85b1-c340bc220532" 13194139535039 true] [17592186328289 1034 "\\pi " 13194139535039 true] [17592186328289 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139535039 true] [17592186328289 1111 #uuid "85e9e631-ccc6-5b2b-9d3a-6262b32beb27" 13194139535039 true] [17592186328290 1034 "1" 13194139535039 true] [17592186328290 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139535039 true] [17592186328290 1111 #uuid "9c2b6e62-e0ac-501d-997f-ec9cd07c6ef5" 13194139535039 true] [17592186328291 1034 "\\frac{3}{2}" 13194139535039 true] [17592186328291 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139535039 true] [17592186328291 1111 #uuid "fe96da0e-5eb2-577d-9db1-e3fccd12593c" 13194139535039 true] [17592186328292 1017 #edb/ref 17592186328293 13194139535039 true] [17592186328292 1089 "q-129644" 13194139535039 true] [17592186328292 1091 #edb/ref 17592186045465 13194139535039 true] [17592186328292 1100 "${\\int }_{-1}^{1}{\\int }_{1}^{2}(x+{y}^{2})\\,\\text{d}y\\,\\text{d}x=$" 13194139535039 true] [17592186328292 1113 #uuid "a687ad08-b4b5-5aee-9377-c64aedd03364" 13194139535039 true] [17592186328292 1145 "First, we evaluate the inner integral by integrating with respect to $y$, treating $x$ as a constant:  \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\int }_{-1}^{1}[{\\int }_{1}^{2}(x+{y}^{2})\\,\\text{d}y]\\text{d}x & ={\\int }_{-1}^{1}\\,{[xy+\\frac{{y}^{3}}{3}]}_{1}^{2}\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & ={\\int }_{-1}^{1}[(2x+\\frac{8}{3})-(x+\\frac{1}{3})]\\text{d}x \\\\  & ={\\int }_{-1}^{1}(x+\\frac{7}{3})\\,\\text{d}x\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThen, we integrate with respect to $x:$ \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\int }_{-1}^{1}(x+\\frac{7}{3})\\,\\text{d}x & ={[\\frac{{x}^{2}}{2}+\\frac{7x}{3}]}_{-1}^{1} \\\\  & =(\\frac{1}{2}+\\frac{7}{3})-(\\frac{1}{2}-\\frac{7}{3}) \\\\  & =\\frac{14}{3}\\end{aligned}\n$$" 13194139535039 true] [17592186328293 1000 #edb/ref 17592186328294 13194139535039 true] [17592186328293 1000 #edb/ref 17592186328295 13194139535039 true] [17592186328293 1000 #edb/ref 17592186328296 13194139535039 true] [17592186328293 1000 #edb/ref 17592186328297 13194139535039 true] [17592186328293 1000 #edb/ref 17592186328298 13194139535039 true] [17592186328293 1040 #edb/ref 17592186045450 13194139535039 true] [17592186328293 1041 "selection" 13194139535039 true] [17592186328293 1104 #edb/ref 17592186328294 13194139535039 true] [17592186328293 1110 #uuid "40157fc0-c0fc-5196-8030-be76f4c42d5d" 13194139535039 true] [17592186328294 1034 "\\frac{14}{3}" 13194139535039 true] [17592186328294 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139535039 true] [17592186328294 1111 #uuid "47b59bc1-a2e3-51ff-a5f0-e8840e10e3b6" 13194139535039 true] [17592186328295 1034 "\\frac{8}{3}" 13194139535039 true] [17592186328295 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139535039 true] [17592186328295 1111 #uuid "2a17e6de-212c-5c19-a087-c7127d5dd99c" 13194139535039 true] [17592186328296 1034 "6" 13194139535039 true] [17592186328296 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139535039 true] [17592186328296 1111 #uuid "7fdd52f9-d9bb-561c-82cc-7d3ff4953215" 13194139535039 true] [17592186328297 1034 "1" 13194139535039 true] [17592186328297 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139535039 true] [17592186328297 1111 #uuid "478dad29-8876-5cf2-8e53-eae1efe9d64b" 13194139535039 true] [17592186328298 1034 "\\frac{1}{3}" 13194139535039 true] [17592186328298 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139535039 true] [17592186328298 1111 #uuid "edd04d7b-dedb-5fda-bed9-bdc414835e4a" 13194139535039 true] [17592186328299 1017 #edb/ref 17592186328300 13194139535039 true] [17592186328299 1089 "q-129645" 13194139535039 true] [17592186328299 1091 #edb/ref 17592186045465 13194139535039 true] [17592186328299 1100 "${\\int }_{0}^{1}{\\int }_{0}^{1}x{e}^{xy}\\,\\text{d}y\\,\\text{d}x=$" 13194139535039 true] [17592186328299 1113 #uuid "19c5efcf-01ef-5fbf-9f64-6c90653aec20" 13194139535039 true] [17592186328299 1145 "First, we evaluate the inner integral by integrating with respect to $y$, treating $x$ as a constant. \n\nMaking a substitution $xy=u,$ $\\text{d}y=\\frac{1}{x}\\,\\text{d}u,$ we get.\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\int }_{0}^{1}[{\\int }_{0}^{1}x{e}^{xy}\\,\\text{d}y]\\text{d}x & ={\\int }_{0}^{1}x[{\\int }_{0}^{1}{e}^{xy}\\,\\text{d}y]\\text{d}x \\\\  & ={\\int }_{0}^{1}x[{\\int }_{0}^{x}\\frac{1}{x}{e}^{u}\\,\\text{d}u]\\text{d}x \\\\  & ={\\int }_{0}^{1}[{\\int }_{0}^{x}{e}^{u}\\,\\text{d}u]\\text{d}x \\\\  & ={\\int }_{0}^{1}[{e}^{u}]_{0}^{x}\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & ={\\int }_{0}^{1}({e}^{x}-1)\\text{d}x\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThen, we integrate with respect to $x:$ \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\int }_{0}^{1}({e}^{x}-1)\\,\\text{d}x & =[{e}^{x}-x]_{0}^{1} \\\\  & =(e-1)-(1-0) \\\\  & =e-2\\end{aligned}\n$$" 13194139535039 true] [17592186328300 1000 #edb/ref 17592186328301 13194139535039 true] [17592186328300 1000 #edb/ref 17592186328302 13194139535039 true] [17592186328300 1000 #edb/ref 17592186328303 13194139535039 true] [17592186328300 1000 #edb/ref 17592186328304 13194139535039 true] [17592186328300 1000 #edb/ref 17592186328305 13194139535039 true] [17592186328300 1040 #edb/ref 17592186045450 13194139535039 true] [17592186328300 1041 "selection" 13194139535039 true] [17592186328300 1104 #edb/ref 17592186328301 13194139535039 true] [17592186328300 1110 #uuid "6e57e113-8971-5956-b522-f72888d2a0ac" 13194139535039 true] [17592186328301 1034 "e-2" 13194139535039 true] [17592186328301 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139535039 true] [17592186328301 1111 #uuid "eb505034-f07c-5969-8499-ba1888c68370" 13194139535039 true] [17592186328302 1034 "2e" 13194139535039 true] [17592186328302 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139535039 true] [17592186328302 1111 #uuid "7b85eead-6ea4-5ffa-9dbf-05336f91eea9" 13194139535039 true] [17592186328303 1034 "e+1" 13194139535039 true] [17592186328303 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139535039 true] [17592186328303 1111 #uuid "54d1cd5a-0eb6-58c9-a9be-42ccd1b1e77e" 13194139535039 true] [17592186328304 1034 "e-1" 13194139535039 true] [17592186328304 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139535039 true] [17592186328304 1111 #uuid "543cbf94-8e83-5ec0-907f-853cffec26f1" 13194139535039 true] [17592186328305 1034 "1-2e" 13194139535039 true] [17592186328305 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139535039 true] [17592186328305 1111 #uuid "e8fb6df7-a4fa-5012-a1ad-833472d48fa0" 13194139535039 true] [17592186328306 1017 #edb/ref 17592186328307 13194139535039 true] [17592186328306 1089 "q-37951" 13194139535039 true] [17592186328306 1091 #edb/ref 17592186045465 13194139535039 true] [17592186328306 1100 "Evaluate the repeated integral\n${\\int }_{-2}^{-1}{\\int }_{0}^{\\sqrt{3}}\\frac{1}{{y}^{2}(1+{x}^{2})}\\,\\text{d}x\\,\\text{d}y.$" 13194139535039 true] [17592186328306 1113 #uuid "c4e727bd-8fd5-54cc-b4fe-00c16c127b2e" 13194139535039 true] [17592186328306 1145 "First, we evaluate the inner integral by integrating with respect to $x$, treating $y$ as a constant:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\int }_{-2}^{-1}[{\\int }_{0}^{\\sqrt{3}}\\frac{1}{{y}^{2}(1+{x}^{2})}\\,\\text{d}x]\\text{d}y & ={\\int }_{-2}^{-1}\\frac{1}{{y}^{2}}[{\\int }_{0}^{\\sqrt{3}}\\frac{1}{(1+{x}^{2})}\\,\\text{d}x]\\text{d}y \\\\  & ={\\int }_{-2}^{-1}\\frac{1}{{y}^{2}}[\\operatorname{arctan}⁡x]_{0}^{\\sqrt{3}}\\,\\text{d}y \\\\  & ={\\int }_{-2}^{-1}\\frac{1}{{y}^{2}}(\\operatorname{arctan}⁡\\sqrt{3}-\\operatorname{arctan}⁡0)\\text{d}y \\\\  & ={\\int }_{-2}^{-1}\\frac{1}{{y}^{2}}(\\frac{\\pi }{3}-0)\\text{d}y \\\\  & ={\\int }_{-2}^{-1}\\frac{\\pi }{3{y}^{2}}\\,\\text{d}y\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThen, we integrate with respect to $y:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\int }_{-2}^{-1}\\frac{\\pi }{3{y}^{2}}\\,\\text{d}y & ={[-\\frac{\\pi }{3y}]}_{-2}^{-1} \\\\  & =-\\frac{\\pi }{3\\cdot (-1)}-(-\\frac{\\pi }{3\\cdot (-2)}) \\\\  & =\\frac{\\pi }{3}-\\frac{\\pi }{6} \\\\  & =\\frac{\\pi }{6}\\end{aligned}\n$$" 13194139535039 true] [17592186328307 1000 #edb/ref 17592186328308 13194139535039 true] [17592186328307 1000 #edb/ref 17592186328309 13194139535039 true] [17592186328307 1000 #edb/ref 17592186328310 13194139535039 true] [17592186328307 1000 #edb/ref 17592186328311 13194139535039 true] [17592186328307 1000 #edb/ref 17592186328312 13194139535039 true] [17592186328307 1040 #edb/ref 17592186045450 13194139535039 true] [17592186328307 1041 "selection" 13194139535039 true] [17592186328307 1104 #edb/ref 17592186328312 13194139535039 true] [17592186328307 1110 #uuid "2e863687-7514-571c-aa1f-454dea7fbfa4" 13194139535039 true] [17592186328308 1034 "-\\frac{\\pi }{3}" 13194139535039 true] [17592186328308 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139535039 true] [17592186328308 1111 #uuid "6cc9376c-f595-5a24-9ea7-535552dcdc52" 13194139535039 true] [17592186328309 1034 "\\frac{1}{6}" 13194139535039 true] [17592186328309 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139535039 true] [17592186328309 1111 #uuid "070fe14f-c904-500e-823c-e55e7b8d1a23" 13194139535039 true] [17592186328310 1034 "\\frac{1}{3}" 13194139535039 true] [17592186328310 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139535039 true] [17592186328310 1111 #uuid "f36ea682-9013-575a-aae0-e8b6d23fccf5" 13194139535039 true] [17592186328311 1034 "0" 13194139535039 true] [17592186328311 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139535039 true] [17592186328311 1111 #uuid "e4692e33-fc62-5914-a8a2-37395d57dc51" 13194139535039 true] [17592186328312 1034 "\\frac{\\pi }{6}" 13194139535039 true] [17592186328312 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139535039 true] [17592186328312 1111 #uuid "409029ae-4dc8-5bf3-b5c8-87c74550a6b7" 13194139535039 true] [17592186328313 1017 #edb/ref 17592186328314 13194139535039 true] [17592186328313 1089 "q-72130" 13194139535039 true] [17592186328313 1091 #edb/ref 17592186045463 13194139535039 true] [17592186328313 1100 "Which of the following equalities are true given that\n$D={(x,y)\\,:\\,1\\le x\\le 2,\\,\\frac{1}{2}\\le y\\le 1}.$\n\n- ${∬}_{D}y\\operatorname{ln}⁡(x)\\,\\text{d}A={\\int }_{1}^{2}{\\int }_{1/2}^{1}y\\operatorname{ln}⁡(x)\\,\\text{d}x\\,\\text{d}y$\n- ${∬}_{D}y\\operatorname{ln}⁡(x)\\,\\text{d}A={\\int }_{1/2}^{1}{\\int }_{1}^{2}y\\operatorname{ln}⁡(x)\\,\\text{d}y\\,\\text{d}x$\n- ${∬}_{D}y\\operatorname{ln}⁡(x)\\text{d}A={\\int }_{1}^{2}{\\int }_{1/2}^{1}y\\operatorname{ln}⁡(x)\\,\\text{d}y\\,\\text{d}x$" 13194139535039 true] [17592186328313 1113 #uuid "81aee10d-0b2a-5edf-957e-80f23e4fc897" 13194139535039 true] [17592186328313 1145 "We notice that:\n\n- the limits for the variable $x$ are from $1$ to $2$, and\n\n- the limits for the variable $y$ are from $\\frac{1}{2}$ to $1.$\n\nTherefore,\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{∬}_{D}y\\operatorname{ln}⁡(x)\\,\\text{d}A & ={\\int }_{1/2}^{1}[{\\int }_{1}^{2}y\\operatorname{ln}⁡(x)\\,\\text{d}x]\\text{d}y.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, since the region of integration is rectangular, we can simply swap the order of integration. This gives\n\n$$\n{∬}_{D}y\\operatorname{ln}⁡(x)\\,\\text{d}A={\\int }_{1}^{2}[{\\int }_{1/2}^{1}y\\operatorname{ln}⁡(x)\\,\\text{d}y]\\text{d}x.\n$$\n\nSo, the correct answer is \"III only\"." 13194139535039 true] [17592186328314 1000 #edb/ref 17592186328315 13194139535039 true] [17592186328314 1000 #edb/ref 17592186328316 13194139535039 true] [17592186328314 1000 #edb/ref 17592186328317 13194139535039 true] [17592186328314 1000 #edb/ref 17592186328318 13194139535039 true] [17592186328314 1000 #edb/ref 17592186328319 13194139535039 true] [17592186328314 1040 #edb/ref 17592186045450 13194139535039 true] [17592186328314 1041 "selection" 13194139535039 true] [17592186328314 1104 #edb/ref 17592186328317 13194139535039 true] [17592186328314 1110 #uuid "1cd3d376-0519-52d1-9277-4a01bb672fba" 13194139535039 true] [17592186328315 1034 "I and III only" 13194139535039 true] [17592186328315 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045454 13194139535039 true] [17592186328315 1111 #uuid "ad446f99-b842-5a1f-9781-495a0a9d2b67" 13194139535039 true] [17592186328316 1034 "I only" 13194139535039 true] [17592186328316 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045454 13194139535039 true] [17592186328316 1111 #uuid "7422fa66-43e0-55d7-9168-7e88966ee1c9" 13194139535039 true] [17592186328317 1034 "III only" 13194139535039 true] [17592186328317 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045454 13194139535039 true] [17592186328317 1111 #uuid "597056b1-7272-5392-a083-d7781bb54a94" 13194139535039 true] [17592186328318 1034 "I and II only" 13194139535039 true] [17592186328318 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045454 13194139535039 true] [17592186328318 1111 #uuid "072bd4be-d5ca-508b-bb03-7d6816e97526" 13194139535039 true] [17592186328319 1034 "II only" 13194139535039 true] [17592186328319 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045454 13194139535039 true] [17592186328319 1111 #uuid "5e90189e-2806-57a2-b52a-fd24ed9e16d1" 13194139535039 true] [17592186328320 1017 #edb/ref 17592186328321 13194139535039 true] [17592186328320 1089 "q-72175" 13194139535039 true] [17592186328320 1091 #edb/ref 17592186045463 13194139535039 true] [17592186328320 1100 "Which of the following equalities are true given that\n$D={(x,y)\\,:\\,0\\le x\\le \\sqrt{2},\\,-\\sqrt{3}\\le y\\le 2}.$\n\n- ${∬}_{D}\\sqrt{1+{x}^{2}{y}^{2}}\\,\\text{d}A={\\int }_{0}^{\\sqrt{2}}{\\int }_{-\\sqrt{3}}^{2}\\sqrt{1+{x}^{2}{y}^{2}}\\,\\text{d}y\\,\\text{d}x$\n- ${∬}_{D}\\sqrt{1+{x}^{2}{y}^{2}}\\,\\text{d}A={\\int }_{-\\sqrt{3}}^{2}{\\int }_{0}^{\\sqrt{2}}\\sqrt{1+{x}^{2}{y}^{2}}\\,\\text{d}x\\,\\text{d}y$\n- ${∬}_{D}\\sqrt{1+{x}^{2}{y}^{2}}\\,\\text{d}A={\\int }_{-\\sqrt{3}}^{2}{\\int }_{0}^{\\sqrt{2}}\\sqrt{1+{x}^{2}{y}^{2}}\\,\\text{d}y\\,\\text{d}x$" 13194139535039 true] [17592186328320 1113 #uuid "80bfbd6a-391f-520f-a0ad-dc736395685b" 13194139535039 true] [17592186328320 1145 "We notice that:  \n\n- the limits for the variable $x$ are from $0$ to $\\sqrt{2}$, and\n\n- the limits for the variable $y$ are from $-\\sqrt{3}$ to $2.$\n\nTherefore,\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{∬}_{D}\\sqrt{1+{x}^{2}{y}^{2}}\\,\\text{d}A & ={\\int }_{-\\sqrt{3}}^{2}[{\\int }_{0}^{\\sqrt{2}}\\sqrt{1+{x}^{2}{y}^{2}}\\,\\text{d}x]\\text{d}y.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, since the region of integration is rectangular, we can simply swap the order of integration. This gives\n\n$$\n{∬}_{D}\\sqrt{1+{x}^{2}{y}^{2}}\\,\\text{d}A={\\int }_{0}^{\\sqrt{2}}[{\\int }_{-\\sqrt{3}}^{2}\\sqrt{1+{x}^{2}{y}^{2}}\\,\\text{d}y]\\text{d}x.\n$$\n\nSo, the correct answer is \"I and II only\"." 13194139535039 true] [17592186328321 1000 #edb/ref 17592186328322 13194139535039 true] [17592186328321 1000 #edb/ref 17592186328323 13194139535039 true] [17592186328321 1000 #edb/ref 17592186328324 13194139535039 true] [17592186328321 1000 #edb/ref 17592186328325 13194139535039 true] [